  "term": "bilingualism",
  "definition": "Bilingualism is the use of two languages by the same people or within the same community. In the source, it is described as a condition that can alter both languages by carrying over the speakers’ usual sound patterns and sentence habits, sometimes blurring the distinct character of each.",
